@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName SansSerif
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam titleFontSize 20
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
skinparam ParticipantPadding 24
skinparam BoxPadding 12
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #42566B
  LifeLineBorderColor #8295A8
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #D8EAFE
  ActivationBorderColor #42566B
  ParticipantBorderColor #42566B
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E8F1FA
  ParticipantFontColor #172B4D
  ActorBorderColor #42566B
  ActorBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  GroupBorderColor #8295A8
  GroupBackgroundColor #F4F7FA
  GroupHeaderFontColor #172B4D
  DividerBackgroundColor #E8F1FA
  DividerBorderColor #8295A8
}
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFBEB
  BorderColor #BBA86A
  FontSize 12
}
hide footbox
title UC-P02 - Submit a Private-EV Charging Request
actor Student as ST
boundary "Student Portal" as UI
control "Charging Request Service" as SVC
entity "Mobility Records" as DATA

note over ST,DATA
  Preconditions: Student is signed in and has a parking reservation or session reference.
  Service calls use the signed-in Student's identity.
end note

ST -> UI: Request charging for a parking booking / session
activate UI #D8EAFE
UI -> SVC: Get charging context (parkingRef)
activate SVC #D8EEDC
SVC -> DATA: Find owned parking context and Hub policy (studentId)
activate DATA #E2E7ED
DATA --> SVC: Owned context and policy / unavailable / retrieval error
deactivate DATA
opt context retrieved
SVC -> SVC: Check eligibility and Hub support; derive permitted charging window
activate SVC #D8EEDC
SVC --> SVC: Eligible context / ineligible / Hub unsupported
deactivate SVC
end
SVC --> UI: Context outcome and permitted window if eligible
deactivate SVC
alt missing, inaccessible or ineligible
UI --> ST: Eligible parking required; return to bookings; disclose no other Student data
else retrieval failed
UI --> ST: Report retrieval error and offer retry
else Hub unsupported
UI --> ST: Charging unavailable at this Hub; keep parking unchanged
else eligible context and supported Hub
UI --> ST: Show vehicle, Hub, charging form and permitted window
end
deactivate UI
break context unavailable, ineligible, unreadable or Hub unsupported
note over ST,DATA
  No charging request created; parking unchanged.
end note
end
note over ST,DATA
  Use Confirmed parking or an Active session for the same Student, vehicle and Hub.
  For Active parking, use the remaining permitted parking interval.
  The requested charging window need not use parking time increments.
end note
ST -> UI: Enter current battery, target battery and requested interval
activate UI #D8EAFE
UI -> SVC: Validate charging inputs and current parking eligibility
activate SVC #D8EEDC
SVC -> DATA: Reload owned parking state and Hub policy
activate DATA #E2E7ED
DATA --> SVC: Current eligibility and policy / retrieval error
deactivate DATA
opt eligible context, supported Hub and verified data
SVC -> SVC: Check 0 <= current < target <= 100; interval within parking window
activate SVC #D8EEDC
SVC --> SVC: Validation result
deactivate SVC
end
SVC --> UI: Validation outcome and request summary if valid
deactivate SVC
alt context invalid, Hub unsupported or data unavailable
UI --> ST: Reject request / report read error; parking unchanged
else eligible context but invalid inputs
UI --> ST: Show field errors; correct battery values or requested interval
else eligible context and valid inputs
UI --> ST: Review request summary; submission does not guarantee a charging slot
end
deactivate UI
break context or inputs invalid, Hub unsupported or retrieval failed
note over ST,DATA
  Revise inputs or reload eligible parking before a new attempt; no creation.
end note
end
ST -> UI: Confirm, edit or abandon charging request
activate UI #D8EAFE
alt Student declines, edits or abandons
UI --> ST: No update; revise inputs with revalidation, or leave
else Student confirms
UI -> SVC: Submit request (parkingRef, inputs, operationRef)
activate SVC #D8EEDC
SVC -> SVC: Recheck session and permission
activate SVC #D8EEDC
SVC --> SVC: Current access result
deactivate SVC
alt session expired or permission denied
SVC -> SVC: Prepare authentication-required / access-denied result
activate SVC #D8EEDC
SVC --> SVC: No update attempted
deactivate SVC
else session valid and permission granted
critical Recheck parking and create one linked request
SVC -> DATA: Create Pending if owned parking, Hub and inputs remain eligible\n(or return equivalent existing active request)
activate DATA #E2E7ED
note over SVC,DATA
  Check Student, vehicle, Hub, battery values and current parking window.
  Serialize with parking cancellation; never leave a live request linked to cancelled parking.
  Allocate no charging slot here.
end note
DATA --> SVC: New Pending / equivalent existing / rejected / save failure
deactivate DATA
end
opt update outcome uncertain / response lost
SVC -> DATA: Find original charging submission result (operationRef, studentId)
activate DATA #E2E7ED
DATA --> SVC: Original result / still unknown
deactivate DATA
end
end
SVC --> UI: Operation outcome and accessible current details
deactivate SVC
alt access invalid
UI --> ST: Sign in if permitted; reload current records and confirm again
else outcome still unknown
UI --> ST: Outcome unconfirmed; retain operationRef and resolve original result before retry
else save failed
UI --> ST: Report failure; no partial update; retry after reload and revalidation
else parking, Hub or inputs no longer eligible
UI --> ST: Reject creation; reload parking and revise request; parking unchanged
else new request created
UI --> ST: Show reference, vehicle, Hub, interval and Pending status
else equivalent active request exists
UI --> ST: Show existing request and status; no duplicate or allocation change
end
end
deactivate UI
note over ST,DATA
  Busy charging points do not prevent an otherwise valid Pending request.
  The scheduler can read the new request; slot assignment is a separate use case.
  Parking remains unchanged throughout this use case.
end note

legend bottom left
  Thin rectangle: execution of a responsibility; nested rectangle: nested execution
  Solid arrow: request / action   |   Dashed arrow: returned result
  Activation ends before waiting for Student input. Read guards top to bottom.
  critical: required consistency boundary; updates are all-or-none as noted
endlegend
footer Smart E-Mobility Hub | Submission 2 | Parking & Private EVs
@enduml
